WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
 Who's got this?

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:02.490
You got this.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.080
Who's out here
cracking b****** up?

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.040
You!

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.020
Is there anybody else like you?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:07.914
No!

00:00:07.914 --> 00:00:08.862
So go kill that shi-

00:00:08.862 --> 00:00:09.810
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:13.080
I wrote a web series called "The
Misadventures of Awkward Black

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.224
Girl," and also wrote a
TV show called "Insecure."

00:00:18.224 --> 00:00:19.652
Shot shot.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.720
Hot s***.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.960
And the only difference
between those two is money.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.540
I'm going to share with
you all of my struggles

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.090
and show you, step
by step, how I

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.890
made the transition
from the internet

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.230
to television and film.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.880
In this class, I
will teach you how

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.710
to collaborate
with other people,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.860
how to build characters,
how to structure a pilot,

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.292
and how to get your
stories out there.

00:00:43.292 --> 00:00:45.000
You have to know where
you want to start.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.670
I wrote the phrase,
"I'm awkward and black,"

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.230
and I was like, aha!

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.674
That's what I've
been this whole time!

00:00:51.674 --> 00:00:52.490
Hey!

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:54.240
I'm going to give you
my blueprint for how

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.550
I wrote my pilot using
four categories: character

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:00.630
setup, conflict,
setting up your series,

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:04.920
and "why today," that
dreaded network question.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.050
I'm a firm believer in
writing what you know.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:10.567
You have to tap into what's
around you and build from that.

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:12.900
If you want to steal your
friend's stories, and then all

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.120
of a sudden, they're
watching an HBO show,

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.160
and they're like, what
the f*** b**** that's me!

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.320
Then that's OK.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.470
When I pitched "Awkward Black
Girl" to a network exec,

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:26.790
he suggested a celebrity actress
who wasn't considered awkward

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.720
at all.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.860
It was just upsetting and clear
to me that he did not get it.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.310
And I had to be comfortable
walking away from that.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.250
If you know the story
you want to tell,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.280
if you know your characters
like the back of your hand,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.890
no one can take
that away from you.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.080
There's an audience for you.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.460
Narrow down the one idea that
you want to pursue right now,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.910
and do it.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:55.050
I'm Issa Rae, and this
is my MasterClass.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:58.100
[MUSIC PLAYING]

